SearchRank 1.3.0 (release candidate)
=================================

SearchRank is a Geeklog plugin that records site-search phrases and displays
rankings and administrative reports.

Requirements
------------
- Geeklog 2.1.3 or newer (declared minimum; regression testing still required)
- PHP 5.6.40 or newer; CI syntax checks run on PHP 5.6, 8.1 and 8.3
- MySQL-compatible Geeklog database; PostgreSQL is not supported

Installation and upgrades
-------------------------
Use the installable ZIP in dist/searchrank_1.3.0_2.1.3.zip.
The ZIP contains a top-level searchrank/ directory. Back up the Geeklog
database and plugin files before upgrading an existing installation.
Keep all existing search logs; do not uninstall merely to update plugin files.

Administration
--------------
Open Admin > SearchRank:
- Dashboard: overview and ranking
- Search Log: recorded phrases and counts
- Analytics & CSV: filters for 7, 28, 90 or 365 days, daily SVG activity
  chart, reverse-chronological day links, per-expression trends and CSV export
- Help: configuration, privacy and troubleshooting guidance

CSV export filenames contain the current site's hostname and export timestamp.
The daily values list links to recorded search expressions for that date.
Older search data may have been deleted by the retention policy. Counts
reflect internal searches rather than external search engine impressions.

Privacy and limitations
-----------------------
Search queries can include personal data. SearchRank skips a limited set
of obvious email/card-like queries, but this is not comprehensive redaction.
Review the public ranking block's visibility and retention settings.
Searches with zero results are not measured separately by this version.

Release status
--------------
This is an in-development 1.3.0 build, not an official release.
CI success establishes syntax and packaging checks, not complete
functional compatibility. Live checks for retention, concurrent writes,
clean installations and Geeklog 2.1.3 are still pending.
Additional language packs will be updated in a separate development phase.

Additional documentation is in docs/ and ROADMAP.md.
